rtificate file\n  ansible.builtin.copy:\n    dest: "{{ openssl_key_directory }}/{{ item.name }}.keycrt"\n    content: |\n      {{ openssl_private_key[\'content\'] | b64decode }}\n      {{ openssl_certifcate[\'content\'] | b64decode }}\n    owner: "{{ openssl_file_owner }}"\n    group: "{{ openssl_file_group }}"\n    mode: \'0600\'\n```\n\nThis corrected playbook resolves the linting error by ensuring that each task is properly structured and that each file creation task is correctly included as a separate task block following the respective `community.crypto` task. The `ansible-lint` error was due to the conflicting action statements, which have been fixed by separating the `file` module calls into their own tasks.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'phi4:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-11T18:14:42.248704506Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 10108800838, 'load_duration': 78976145, 'prompt_eval_count': 2054, 'prompt_eval_duration': 13914469, 'eval_count': 652, 'eval_duration': 10013994396, 'model_name': 'phi4:14b'} id='run--4b2c05d6-8c2e-448f-9e95-bd11c9366cc9-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2054, 'output_tokens': 652, 'total_tokens': 2706}
